# Copy to .env and fill in what you need. .env is gitignored and must stay that
# way: every value below is a live credential.
#
# This file is NOT how the local stack is configured. `make up` generates the
# stack's own variables — ports, uid, secret paths — into .env.stack, and
# regenerates them on every run. Nothing here is required to bring the stack up
# or to run `make test`; .env exists only so the acceptance suites can reach a
# venue, and every one of them skips with the name of the variable it wanted
# rather than failing when it is absent.
#
# Read by internal/testenv.LoadRepoEnv, which loads this file into the test
# process's environment. A variable already set in your shell always wins.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Write gates.
#
# Every acceptance suite is read-only until one of these is set to 1. With a gate
# on, that suite places real orders on the venue's demo or testnet exchange using
# the credentials below — bounded by the MAX_NOTIONAL values further down, but
# real orders on a real matching engine nonetheless. Leave them unset unless you
# mean it, and turn them back off afterwards.
#
# These are the one class of variable this file does not deliver: internal/testenv
# refuses to import any key beginning ENABLE_/ALLOW_/RUN_ from .env, precisely so
# that a gate cannot be left switched on in a file and forgotten. Pass them on the
# command line instead, where they are visible in the command that used them:
#
#   BOLTER_ENABLE_BINANCE_DEMO_WRITES=1 make test-gateway-binance-spot-demo
#
# The full set, for reference — they are listed, not assigned:
#   BOLTER_ENABLE_BINANCE_DEMO_WRITES        BOLTER_ENABLE_OKX_DEMO_WRITES
#   BOLTER_ENABLE_BITGET_DEMO_WRITES         BOLTER_ENABLE_BYBIT_DEMO_WRITES
#   BOLTER_ENABLE_BYBIT_TESTNET_WRITES       BOLTER_ENABLE_GATE_TESTNET_WRITES
#   BOLTER_ENABLE_HYPERLIQUID_TESTNET_WRITES BOLTER_ENABLE_LIGHTER_TESTNET_WRITES
#   BOLTER_ENABLE_ASTER_TESTNET_WRITES       BOLTER_ENABLE_NADO_TESTNET_WRITES
#   BOLTER_ALLOW_OKX_DEMO_CUSTOM_WRITES      BOLTER_ALLOW_BITGET_DEMO_CUSTOM_WRITES
#   BOLTER_ENABLE_LIVE_READ_TESTS

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binance — the MVP venue. This pair alone is enough for the manual order loop
# the stack is built around; everything below it is optional breadth.
#
# Keys come from testnet.binance.vision (spot) and testnet.binancefuture.com
# (futures), not from binance.com. A mainnet key here reaches a mainnet
# matching engine.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
BINANCE_DEMO_API_KEY=
BINANCE_DEMO_API_SECRET=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The other venues. Each block is all-or-nothing: a suite skips unless every
# variable in its block is set.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

OKX_DEMO_API_KEY=
OKX_DEMO_API_SECRET=
OKX_DEMO_API_PASSPHRASE=

# BITGET_DEMO_SECRET_KEY, not _API_SECRET — Bitget's own naming, kept as-is.
# The older BITGET_TESTNET_* spelling of this block still works: testenv aliases
# each one onto its BITGET_DEMO_* equivalent, and the canonical name wins when
# both are set. New setups should use the names below.
BITGET_DEMO_API_KEY=
BITGET_DEMO_SECRET_KEY=
BITGET_DEMO_PASSPHRASE=

BYBIT_DEMO_API_KEY=
BYBIT_DEMO_API_SECRET=

BYBIT_TESTNET_API_KEY=
BYBIT_TESTNET_API_SECRET=

GATE_TESTNET_API_KEY=
GATE_TESTNET_API_SECRET=

# The wallet-signed venues. These are private keys, not API keys: anything they
# sign for is spendable, so use a wallet funded only with testnet assets.
HYPERLIQUID_TESTNET_PK=

LIGHTER_TESTNET_PRIVATE_KEY=
LIGHTER_TESTNET_ACCOUNT_INDEX=
LIGHTER_TESTNET_API_KEY_INDEX=

ASTER_TESTNET_USER_ADDRESS=
ASTER_TESTNET_SIGNER_PRIVATE_KEY=

NADO_TESTNET_PRIVATE_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bounds and overrides, all optional.
#
# Every venue has a max-notional ceiling with a small built-in default, and most
# also accept symbol, REST base URL and WS URL overrides for pointing a suite at
# a different instrument or a mirror. internal/testenv/testenv.go is the list; it
# names each one beside the default it falls back to. Set one only when the
# default is wrong for you.
#
# The ceiling is worth raising deliberately and lowering again — it is the last
# thing between a mistyped quantity and an order the venue actually fills. Note
# the quote asset is part of the name and differs per venue.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OKX_DEMO_MAX_NOTIONAL_USDT=
# BYBIT_DEMO_MAX_NOTIONAL_USDT=
# HYPERLIQUID_TESTNET_MAX_NOTIONAL_USDC=
# NADO_TESTNET_MAX_NOTIONAL_USDT0=
